            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BOI02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Chastel</forename>
                        <surname>De Boinville</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>soldier</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The Boinville family had a long association with the Godwins. Chastel de Boinville married <persName key="BOI01">Harriet Boinville</persName> whose 
      father had been involved in Godwin's and <persName key="MAR01">Marshall's</persName> ventures in the West Indies in the 1780s. Harriet became an 
      enthusiastic disciple of the New Philosophy and the families became close in the 1800s. The Boinvilles were close friends of the <persName key="NEW01">Newtons</persName>, 
      another family of fervent Godwinians.</p>
                        <p>For a fuller discussion see <persName key="BOI01">Harriet Boinville</persName></p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
